# Modern UI (Mobile-First + Tailwind + SCSS)

Prefer a modern, clean UI. Build **mobile-first**, then enhance with breakpoints (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:`). Use Tailwind for layout utilities in markup. Use SCSS for component styles, and **always** pull values from the shared variable files — never hard-code colors, sizes, or fonts that already exist as tokens.

## SCSS & Design Tokens

Token files live under `src/lib/styles/variables/`:

- `_colors.scss` — colors
- `_sizes.scss` — spacing, radius, container/touch sizes
- `_fonts.scss` — font family, sizes, weights, line heights
- `_index.scss` — forwards all of the above

**Source of truth is Tailwind theme scales.** SCSS variables must alias Tailwind CSS variables — never hard-code hex, rem, or px:

- Colors → semantic `$color-*` / `var(--color-brand)` (Obsidian Volt: slate + cyan — see `color-palette.mdc`), never raw hex
- Spacing → `calc(var(--spacing) * N)`
- Type → `var(--text-sm)`, `var(--font-weight-semibold)`, `var(--leading-normal)`, `var(--tracking-tight)`
- Radius → `var(--radius-md)`, containers → `var(--container-6xl)`
- Breakpoints (SCSS `@media` only) → `$breakpoint-sm` / `md` / `lg` / `xl` (match Tailwind `--breakpoint-*`)

Semantic CSS custom properties are emitted from `src/lib/styles/tokens.scss` (imported in the root layout).

### Required patterns

- Component styles use `<style lang="scss">` (not plain CSS).
- At the top of every SCSS block/file that needs tokens: `@use 'lib/styles/variables' as *;`
- Reference `$color-*`, `$space-*`, `$font-*`, `$radius-*`, `$size-*`, `$breakpoint-*`.
- If a value is missing, **add a Tailwind-aliased token** in the correct variables file first. Do not invent local magic numbers.

```svelte
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<style>
	.panel {
		color: #0f172a;
		padding: 17px;
		font-size: 15px;
	}
</style>

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<style lang="scss">
	@use 'lib/styles/variables' as *;

	.panel {
		color: $color-text;
		padding: $space-4;
		font-size: $font-size-sm;
	}
</style>
```

## Layout & Responsiveness

- Default styles target small screens; add larger breakpoints only when needed.
- Prefer flex/grid + gap over fixed widths and absolute positioning.
- Use fluid containers (`w-full`, `max-w-*`, `mx-auto`) and percentage/fr-based layouts.
- Touch targets and stacking should work on narrow viewports before desktop refinements.

```svelte
<!-- ❌ BAD: desktop-first, fixed width -->
<div class="w-[960px] flex-row gap-[18px]">...</div>

<!-- ✅ GOOD: mobile-first, fluid -->
<div class="flex w-full max-w-6xl flex-col gap-4 md:flex-row md:gap-6">...</div>
```

## Spacing, Sizing & Units

- Prefer Tailwind utilities in markup (`p-4`, `gap-6`, `text-sm`, `bg-[var(--color-brand)]`) and SCSS `$` aliases of those same theme tokens in `<style lang="scss">`.
- Never introduce raw hex / rem / px in variable files — alias Tailwind theme CSS variables instead.
- Prefer relative/fluid units: `%`, `fr`, `svh`/`dvh`, `max-w-*` + `w-full`.
- Reserve arbitrary Tailwind values (`[]`) for rare cases; if a value repeats, add a Tailwind-aliased SCSS token.

## Visual Quality

- Keep hierarchy clear: one primary action per section, restrained color, consistent type scale.
- Prefer shared color/spacing/font tokens over one-off palettes. Follow Obsidian Volt (`color-palette.mdc`).
- Do not introduce dense card grids, pill clusters, or decorative chrome unless the interaction needs it.
- Ensure layouts remain usable without horizontal scroll on common phone widths.
